most interestingly, auroc2 and M-ratio produce completely inverted model rankings, demonstrating

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:41.480
their measuring fundamentally different things. Let's pop the hood for a moment on that pruning paper

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:47.860
because the representation hierarchy's insight is genuinely useful for practitioners. Everyone talks

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:52.940
about pruning like it's a simple switch you flip. In reality, it's a story about three different

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:58.740
representation spaces reacting differently to the same perturbation. Embeddings and logits are

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:05.320
remarkably robust. The danger zone is the non-linear jump into probability space where small errors get

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:10.480
amplified and then accumulate across every token in generation. This gives you a clear decision

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:15.620
